      "HullValue": 64743724,
      "ModulesValue": 9774469,
      "UnladenMass": 699,
      "CargoCapacity": 8,
      "MaxJumpRange": 17.49517,
      "FuelCapacity": {
        "Main": 16,
        "Reserve": 0.83
      },
      "Rebuy": 3725909
    },
    "journalTolerance": {
      "note": "The journal rounds; these are the source event's own figures, matched within 1e-4. Nothing on this build is engineered, so agreement is agreement with the catalogue's own module masses and drive stats.",
      "UnladenMass": 699.0,
      "MaxJumpRange": 17.495169
    },
    "ammunition": {
      "note": "The game reports the loaded weapons' magazine and reserve, which is one of two external checks on `clipSize` and `ammoMaximum` a journal gives; the other, stronger one is the `AmmoClipSize` / `AmmoMaximum` modifier an engineered module states. Both weapons are sitting at capacity, so each figure below is also what a parsed build reports for that weapon. Only the two weapons carrying ammo at capture time say anything — the other four report zero on both counts, which is a fact about this ship's rearm state and not about the catalogue, so they are not pinned. The counts themselves are read off the capture rather than off a parsed build, because a build carries no rearm state: `AmmoInClip` and `AmmoInHopper` are dropped on import by design, and what a weapon can hold is reported from the catalogue stats instead.",
      "loaded": [
        {
          "symbol": "Hpt_ATMultiCannon_Fixed_Large_V2",
          "AmmoInClip": 100,
          "AmmoInHopper": 2100
        },
        {
          "symbol": "Hpt_Guardian_ShardCannon_Fixed_Large",
          "AmmoInClip": 5,
          "AmmoInHopper": 180
        }
      ]
    },
    "discount": {
      "note": "All 18 priced modules were bought at 0.8775 of catalogue list, each within a credit after the game's own rounding — a second, independent reading of the price table beside the Viper Mk IV's flat 0.85, at a different discount. The residual credit splits cleanly: the 12 internals land exactly on the floor of the ratio, the six hardpoints one credit above it, which is a rounding rule this repository does not model and does not need to. The hull agrees with the Viper Mk IV rather than the Krait Phantom: 56801651 is below even the bare `hullCost` and is 0.8775 of neither convention, so a journal's HullValue is not a second reading of the price table and none of these figures is carried through.",
      "sourceHullValue": 56801651,
      "sourceModulesValue": 8577094,
      "sourceRebuy": 3268938,
      "hullRetailCost": 67527359,
      "hullCost": 64743724,
      "moduleDiscount": 0.8775,
      "moduleDiscountToleranceCr": 1,
      "pricedInSource": 18,
      "rebuyFromOwnFigures": 3268937,
      "unpricedInSource": ["Armour", "CargoHatch"]
    }
  },
